  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**Q3) OR B):** In a data processing pipeline, you are given a list of numerical identifiers. As a part of the data validation process, you need to filter this list to keep only the identifiers that are prime numbers.\n\nDefine a function that accepts a list and returns a new list containing only the prime numbers from the original list, maintaining their original order.\n\n**Rules:**\n\n\nA prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself.\nYour function must handle lists that may contain non-integer values, negative numbers, 0, and 1. These should be excluded from the final list.\nThe solution must be implemented using a `for` loop and conditional statements.\n\nInput Format\n\nInput contains a list of integral and non-integral values.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nA Python list containing only the prime numbers inside square brackets.",
